<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40959" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστᾰδόν</span></b> , Adv., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφίστημι, ἐπιστῆναι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>standing over each in turn</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφιστάμενος ἑκάστῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>EM</u>
					364.35
				</span></i>
			), i.e. <i>one after another, successively</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νείκεον ἄλλοθεν ἄλλον ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.392
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νώμησεν δ᾽ ἄρα πᾶσιν
			ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				13.54
			</span></i>; <i>standing by</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.293
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. οὐτάζοντες</span>
			<i>standing up to</i> each other, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.84
			</span></i>.—The words of <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.453
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόρπον ἐ. ὡπλίζοντο</span>,
			seem to have given rise to the other expl. of the Sch., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισταμένως, ἐμπείρως</span> (as if from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίσταμαι</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
